From 2dbf8e6714d099d7058f463028b98a0f13d45222 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:31:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gluon-core: nominate LAN1 as the uplink on the FRITZ!Box 7560

The FRITZ!Box 7560 has no WAN jack, so OpenWrt's board.d declares all
four front-panel sockets as LAN and board.json carries no wan role.
020-interfaces then leaves wan_ifname nil, all four ports become
single_ifname, and 021-interface-roles gives that single interface the
WAN roles. The node comes up with every socket in br-wan and no Ethernet
port in br-client.

Gluon already handles avm,fritz7430 and avm,fritzbox-7530 by nominating
LAN1, so do the same here. lan1 is the socket marked LAN 1. Each DSA
port carries the label of the socket it reaches, whatever the internal
port numbering.

The result is one uplink port and three client ports, in two
gluon.interface sections whose roles can be changed independently in
config mode. The two bridges stay apart. Every user port carries an
ingress rule that puts it in its bridge's forwarding domain, and the
switch forwards known unicast only within that domain. It hands every
other frame to the processor, whose software bridge keeps it inside
br-wan or br-client. A port in neither bridge is fenced from both.

This does not re-role a deployed node. When 021-interface-roles migrates
iface_single, it copies that section's role onto both new sections, so a
node already in the field keeps all four ports as uplink until the roles
are set in config mode.

The FRITZ!Box 7580 and 7590 need no entry. Both have a WAN jack, board.d
gives it the wan role, and 020-interfaces finds both names on its own.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
---
 package/gluon-core/luasrc/lib/gluon/upgrade/020-interfaces | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/gluon-core/luasrc/lib/gluon/upgrade/020-interfaces b/package/gluon-core/luasrc/lib/gluon/upgrade/020-interfaces
index 6a2568b9..e4b33c1a 100755
--- a/package/gluon-core/luasrc/lib/gluon/upgrade/020-interfaces
+++ b/package/gluon-core/luasrc/lib/gluon/upgrade/020-interfaces
@@ -88,6 +88,10 @@ elseif platform.match('lantiq', 'xrx200', {
 	'avm,fritz7430',
 }) then
 	lan_ifname, wan_ifname = 'lan2 lan3 lan4', 'lan1'
+elseif platform.match('intel-mips', 'xrx500', {
+	'avm,fritz7560',
+}) then
+	lan_ifname, wan_ifname = 'lan2 lan3 lan4', 'lan1'
 elseif platform.match('lantiq', 'xrx200', {
 	'arcadyan,vgv7510kw22-nor',
 }) then
